  "overall_explanation": "Most sensitive actions are role-gated, but the upgradeable initialization flow is the primary exploitable risk: if the proxy is ever left uninitialized, any external account can seize admin/manager privileges and set an attacker-controlled liquidity buffer, then drain all Aave-backed funds through the normal `withdraw()` path. Other powerful functions are restricted to privileged roles and are not exploitable without privileged-role compromise."
